# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/


# Secrets: never commit OAuth credentials or keys
oauth.toml
client_secret*.json
*.key
.env

# Added by cargo

/target

# Built setup executables. The published one comes from CI, not from here.
/dist

# Python bytecode from the asset scripts
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Mutation testing output. Regenerated by scripts/mutants.sh.
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/

# Pages made from the documents at run time, so the help button opens HTML
# rather than raw Markdown. Generated beside their sources, never edited.
docs/*.html

# GSD Core's own tooling, installed by
# `npx @opengsd/gsd-core@latest --claude --local --profile=full`.
# Thirteen megabytes of vendored framework that any checkout can reinstall,
# so it does not belong in the history. What is NOT ignored, deliberately:
#
#   .claude/guardrails/  ours, with its own tests. It is a guard like the
#                          ones in guards/, and a guard nobody can see is a
#                          guard nobody maintains.
#   .claude/skills/      ours, already tracked.
#   .planning/           GSD's planning artifacts are meant to live with the
#                          repo and be reviewed like any other document.
.claude/agents/
.claude/commands/
.claude/gsd-core/
.claude/hooks/
.claude/scripts/
.claude/gsd-migration-journal/
.claude/gsd-file-manifest.json
# Where the harness puts a subagent's git worktree. Transient, and it holds a
# whole checkout with its own build directory: the one left on 2026-09-02 was
# 293MB. Untracked and unignored, it is a trap for `git add -A`, and it is
# nested deeply enough that `git worktree remove` failed on it with "Filename
# too long" and it had to be deleted through the extended-path prefix.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/gsd-install-state.json
.claude/.gsd-profile
.claude/.gsd-runtime
.claude/VERSION

# The phase researcher's web-fetch cache. Content, not decisions: the pages it
# read are quoted in RESEARCH.md, which is tracked. Caching them again here
# would put a few hundred kilobytes of somebody else's HTML in the history.
.planning/research/.cache/

# GSD runtime state, not decisions. `.gsd/` holds the dispatch-isolation
# sentinel the guard hooks read, which is per-run and per-machine.
# `milestone.lock` is held while a milestone command runs. Neither is a record
# of anything; both are regenerated, and both would conflict on every merge.
.gsd/
.planning/milestone.lock

# Written by scripts/check.sh when a red commit is not the red it claimed,
# so the whole run can be read after the commit was refused.
red-run.log
